Subject: [PATCH] arm64: a platform symbol and a dts directory for the Z500KL

MACH_ASUS_Z500KL selects this tablet the way MACH_SONY_SUZU selects the Xperia
X: arch/arm64/boot/dts/asus/Makefile builds the tablet's device tree when it is
set, and the image carries only that one appended. Like Sony's, it depends on
ARCH_MSM8916, under which this tree builds the MSM8956.
---
--- arch/arm64/Kconfig.platforms
+++ arch/arm64/Kconfig.platforms
@@ -380,6 +380,13 @@ config MACH_SONY_SUZU
 	  If you enable this config,
 	  please use SONY Mobile device tree.
 
+config MACH_ASUS_Z500KL
+	bool "ASUS ZenPad 3S 10 LTE (Z500KL)"
+	depends on ARCH_MSM8916
+	help
+	  Support for the ASUS ZenPad 3S 10 LTE, Z500KL (ASUS_P00I),
+	  a tablet built on the MSM8956.
+
 config MACH_SONY_KUGO
 	bool "Sony Mobile Kugo"
 	depends on ARCH_SONY_LOIRE
--- arch/arm64/boot/dts/Makefile
+++ arch/arm64/boot/dts/Makefile
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@ dts-dirs += altera
 dts-dirs += amd
 dts-dirs += amlogic
 dts-dirs += apm
+dts-dirs += asus
 dts-dirs += arm
 dts-dirs += broadcom
 dts-dirs += cavium
